1. DEFINITIONS

"Licensor" means the copyright holder named above, the owner of the Veystrix
components that the Licensor authored, as described in section 6.

"Software" means the Veystrix macOS application and the Veystrix inference
engine helper bundled inside it, in the unmodified form published by the
Licensor as an "Official Build" at
https://github.com/joyboyreturns/Veystrix/releases, including any update the
Licensor publishes through the application's update feed.

"Official Build" means a file published by the Licensor at the address above
whose SHA-256 checksum matches the checksum the Licensor published for it. When
the release notes state that a build is signed with the Licensor's Developer ID
and notarized by Apple, its code signature must also verify. A build that the
release notes describe as "free build, not notarized" is signed ad hoc and is an
Official Build on the strength of its checksum alone; macOS will warn when you
first open it.

"Model Checkpoint" means a machine-learning model, weights or tokenizer that you
obtain from anyone other than the Licensor. Model Checkpoints are not part of
the Software.

"You" means the individual or organization that installs or uses the Software.

"Personal Use" means use of the Software by an individual for their own private,
non-commercial purposes, on a computer they own or control, and expressly
includes benchmarking, performance testing, research, evaluation, education and
personal experimentation, and use of the text the Software generates for those
purposes.

"Business Use" means any use of the Software by or on behalf of a company,
corporation, partnership, sole trader, non-profit organization, government
body, university department, or other organization.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software that is not Personal Use,
including any use:
(a) on equipment, an account, a network or time paid for or provided by an
    employer, client or other organization, or during working hours for an
    organization;
(b) as part of, or in support of, a product, service, subscription, offering or
    internal business process;
(c) for or in connection with consulting, contract work, or a client or customer
    engagement, or any work billed or charged to a third party;
(d) that generates revenue or other commercial benefit, or reduces costs, for
    an individual or organization; or
(e) where the Software or its output is sold, licensed or made available to a
    third party for consideration.
Business Use and Commercial Use overlap; either one requires the paid commercial
license described in section 3.

