7. MODEL CHECKPOINTS

The Software does not include model weights and does not download them without
Your explicit action. A Model Checkpoint is licensed by its publisher, not by
the Licensor. You are responsible for reading and following the license of any
checkpoint You use.

8. PRIVACY

The Software does not require an account and does not send Your prompts,
files, repositories, sessions or model data to the Licensor or any third party.
The only network access the Software makes by itself is the optional update
check, which You can turn off in Settings; it requests the public update feed
from github.com and sends no information about Your prompts or files. Your
Internet provider and GitHub can see ordinary connection metadata (such as Your
IP address) when You check for updates, as with any web request. Network
features of tools You connect to the local server (for example coding agents)
are controlled by those tools, not by the Software.

9. NO WARRANTY, SAFETY AND LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

The Software streams very large model files from Your SSD and can use most of
the memory of Your computer. This reads many gigabytes per request, can increase
SSD wear, and can slow or interrupt other applications. The Software includes
memory and swap protections, but they are estimates and cannot guarantee that
Your computer will not become slow or unresponsive. Keep Your computer on AC
power during long sessions and keep backups of important data.

Output generated by language models can be wrong, unsafe or offensive. You are
responsible for checking it before You rely on it.

